DECISION
AR-H115 is POSITIVE WITH PERSISTENCE-GATE MEMORY DISCIPLINE.

Supported synthetically:

- persistent local residuals can earn local predictive models;
- local prediction sharply reduces repeated communication;
- local model birth need not rewrite the global model;
- local model authority can be suppressed quickly when its context ends;
- brief transient anomalies do not automatically create model memory;
- the same region can later earn a model if the anomaly becomes persistent.

Not demonstrated:

- unsupervised arbitrary residual-region geometry;
- dormant model reactivation;
- local model overlap;
- memory pricing across many exception models;
- context hierarchy deeper than two levels;
- real perceptual content.

